00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.230
Every time Pennywise Was In The Background
Of IT

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.230
________________

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:06.000
Ok so the first appearance of Pennywise actually
comes within the first five minutes of the

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.770
movie, way before Georgie has his fateful
run in with the killer clown in the sewers.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.329
As Georgie makes his way down to the basement
he passes several impressions of Pennywise

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:22.889
and even almost bumps into the character directly
when making his way down the stairs to the

00:01:22.889 --> 00:01:23.889
bottom part of the house.

00:01:23.889 --> 00:01:27.149
In addition to this, it looks like Pennywise
may be a painter and decorator on the side

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:33.149
as in his home there are several small images
of Pennywise engrained into the wallpaper.

00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:36.700
Just before Georgie goes down the steps into
the basement in a blink and you'll miss it

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.130
moment that roughly takes place over two frames,
you may also notice his small shiny eyes watching

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.189
the young boy at the top of the stairs as
he descends into the flight of steps.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.679
Whilst he also appears later in the scene,
hiding under the stairs, this is the first

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:55.189
of many examples that show that he's always
one step behind his prey, constantly stalking

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:57.630
them and waiting for the perfect moment to
attack.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.869
Who knows how long he followed Georgie for
during this scene but it's enough to give

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:06.950
you Goosebumps as you realise that once Pennywise
has it's eyes on you it's difficult to get

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:07.950
away.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:08.950
3

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:09.950
The Library Scene
________________

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.239
Up next is the Library scene with Ben in which
there are several minor appearances by Pennywise

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:16.430
before he makes his final play and tries to
attack the character in the basement of the

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.430
building.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.461
I guess the rule is, if there's a killer clown
after you, just don't go downstairs anywhere.

00:02:20.461 --> 00:02:26.110
Anyway, the first one comes in the form of
the creepy librarian that slowly watches Ben

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.269
as he reads about the history of Derry.

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:32.510
Throughout the scene the mysterious librarian
creepily stares at him, smiling as he digs

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.430
deeper into what exactly may be going on in
the town.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.410
It's a really haunting scene and is something
that I didn't even pick up on my first couple

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:43.340
of watches though the more you focus on the
background of the scene, the more that you

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.000
realise that Pennywise is slowly making his
play.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.670
I noticed comments last time of people saying
it was just the woman doing her job but she's

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.420
also standing in the exact same position that
the Balloon appears in in the next shot that

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.989
leads Ben to go down into the Basement which
cements for me that the character is indeed

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:01.989
taking on her form.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:02.989
it chapter 2 easter eggs explained every time
pennywise was in the background of a scene

00:03:02.989 --> 00:03:03.989
things you missed post credits scene trivia

00:03:03.989 --> 00:03:06.540
Another blink and you'll miss it moment also
happens in this scene when Ben is flicking

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.209
through the book, in a small frame that flies
by so fast you have to screenshot it in order

00:03:11.209 --> 00:03:16.030
to see it, you will see the children's Easter
egg hunt that infamously ended in disaster.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.269
In the top corner of the photo when paused
you will notice a blurry vision of Pennywise

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:25.590
that shows he was the cause behind the massacre
and has been in the town at several key points.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:31.510
As we know from IT, Pennywise is often at
the centre of many famous disasters in Derry

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:35.079
and this confirms that he was indeed behind
the many deaths in the Easter Egg hunt.

00:03:35.079 --> 00:03:36.079
5a

00:03:36.079 --> 00:03:37.079
Ben Gets Bullied
________________

00:03:37.079 --> 00:03:40.120
Soon after this scene, Ben is caught by Henry
Bowers and we see a balloon pop up in the

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.520
back window of a car.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.790
During the attack as he calls out for help
which goes completely unnoticed.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.379
This shows that Pennywise has a hold over
the adults in Derry and is psychically controlling

00:03:49.379 --> 00:03:53.219
them so that they will appear nonchalant to
any trouble that children in the area get

00:03:53.219 --> 00:03:54.219
into.

00:03:54.219 --> 00:03:58.329
This is why Beverly's father can't see the
blood in the bathroom and why in one of the

00:03:58.329 --> 00:04:02.560
film's many deleted scene's Bill's father
is unable to see that the basement is flooded

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.670
after the encounter with Georgie and Pennywise
down there.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:09.989
It's also why no one really ever leaves Derry
and the fact that most of The Losers do shows

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:14.010
that they are highly driven people which plays
into why they all go on to have successful

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:15.010
careers.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:19.610
Though the one in the car is rather obvious
it adds a nice amount of subtext to the city

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.350
and definitely lets you know that Pennywise
has the ability to reach into pretty much

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.610
every aspect of Derry.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:25.610
Ben's Wound
________________

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.130
The next one comes during the scene in which
the Losers Club try and help Ben with his

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.130
cuts.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.310
The characters are all leaning up against
a wall with graffiti behind then which seems

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:38.880
innocuous enough until, during the scene,
Pennywise's face appears in the markings watching

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.880
them.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.220
The face definitely isn't there earlier in
the scene so it's safe to say that this has

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.850
been done with something else other than a
spray can.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.950
It's an awesome little addition that once
again cements just how able Pennywise is with

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:54.500
hunting his prey, he can follow them wherever
he wants to and this makes him infinitely

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.500
more terrifying.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.370
A similar appearance happens in Chapter 2
as well with the character reappearing in

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:02.790
the graffiti after not being there the first
time that we pass it.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.790
6

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:04.790
The Fair
________________

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:08.060
Up next is another rather obvious one but
I thought I'd include it in case you missed

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.060
it.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.860
During the scene in which the losers club
all admit that they are afraid of something,

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:16.150
we can see a clown on the stage in the background
staring at the group and when Richie says

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:20.540
that he hates clown, the figure reaches out
menacingly to him with a balloon and from

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.570
this point out just stares at him.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:27.300
Yep, that's Pennywise alright and this scene
is given more weight in IT Chapter Two when

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.240
Bill rides past the same location and Pennywise
can still be seen poking out from under the

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.240
car.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.240
The TV Show
________________

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:36.060
Beverly has a doll that looks similar to Pennywise
and the character also makes an appearance

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.480
in the TV show that seems to be plastered
across every television screen in Derry.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:46.120
Whilst Pennywise definitely appears at the
end, taunting Henry to kill his own father,

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.360
if you go back and watch the movie you will
notice that this show also appears in the

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.850
rest of the film throughout the entire town.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:58.120
Firstly Eddie's mother is sat watching it
when the children go out, later when Beverly

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:09.300
sneaks past her father, he too is watching
it.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:13.580
This is another way that Pennywise slowly
seeps into the consciousness of the town and

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.260
why so many kids end up going to the sewers
to play.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:20.020
You might also notice that sitting next to
the presenter are the missing children from

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:24.140
Derry who all have severe wounds in their
body that probably indicate the brutal way

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.550
that Pennywise killed them.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.410
This show is just another way for Pennywise
to hunt and we know that Pennywise is psychically

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:33.111
pushing it into the townspeoples minds as
we see Beverly sneak past it once and then

00:06:33.111 --> 00:06:36.070
when she goes past it again the tv is just
playing static.

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.070
Yikes.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.070
It Chapter 2 Hidden Pennywise scenes

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.070
Bob Gray Bottle
________________

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.860
On the way to the house on Neobolt Street,
before they enter we can see a bottle with

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:46.300
Bob Gray on it that has a callback to Pennywise
who famously used to use the moniker.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:50.640
Bob Gray is a reference to the serial killer
Albert Fish who too used the pseudonym when

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.710
carrying out his killings which involved kidnapping
and cannibalism.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:54.710
The Doll
________________

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:59.150
The final one for the film comes in the house
on Neobolt Street in which Richie becomes

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:00.660
trapped in a room full of Dolls.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:05.730
Not only is there a one that resembles the
original IT portrayal by Tim Curry in the

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:10.140
1990s mini-series, there's also one that looks
like Pennywise on the right-hand side.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:14.240
Both sides of the room show the history of
Pennywise and it showcases that the character

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.930
was watching Richie far before he jumped out
of the coffin to attack him.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:22.370
Ok so that's all of the ones for It Chapter
One now let's move onto It Chapter 2.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.370
It Chapter 2 Hidden Pennywise
________________

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:27.500
The first one we see in It Chapter 2 is during
the introductory logos in which we can see

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:32.180
the deadlights floating around the Warner
Bros and New Line Logo letting us know that

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.290
these will be major parts of the film.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:38.810
This is Pennywise's true form and it's awesome
that we kick start the film with a nod towards

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.640
the creatures real appearance.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:44.160
Another brilliant thing that It Chapter 2
does that the prior film didn't is that it

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:48.120
engrains the symbolism of Pennywise into several
aspects of the town.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.560
The parade is littered with Red Balloons,
and then there is a huge mass of them that

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.300
appears under the bridge after he is attacked.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.480
This shot is then mirrored slightly later
on when the girl leaves the bleachers as many

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:02.640
of the members of the crowd wear red hats
and due to their positioning they almost look

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.360
like balloons arching down.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.690
A Red Balloon also pops up behind Adrian at
the Carnival before he's attacked and the

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:17.410
actor who plays Chris Unwin who takes part
in the attack, Katie Lunman also played the

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:21.900
part of Betty Ripson in the first film who
was one of Pennywise's victims.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:28.110
This recasting was done intentionally as in
Derry, those who die horrible deaths at the

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:33.430
hands of Pennywise don't get to go to an afterlife,
instead their doomed spirits remain in the

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.900
town, being reincarnated and then going on
to live hateful lives.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:42.900
Mike mentions that it's like an echo, bouncing
back every 27 years and for those who don't

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:48.000
know, this character was sentenced to prison
after the attack, having his life ended in

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.400
some ways round about the same time that Betty
had hers.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.520
Anyway, this not the only recasting either
as Eddie's wife is also played by the same

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.930
actress that played his mother in the first
film.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.750
This was put in place to show that Eddie did
literally marry his mother in some ways and

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.940
there is a big part in the book that jokes
about how similar his wife and mother are.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:10.990
Other cameos include Stephen King and the
Director of the film Andy Muschetti who appears

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:13.480
behind Eddie during his return to the Pharmacy.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.940
Beverly's Painting
________________

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:20.940
In Beverly's home we see he run past a large
painting of her and her husband Tom Rogan.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:25.400
Over Tom's shoulder you can see the almost
shadowy form of Pennywise almost controlling

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.400
him.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:30.500
Pennywise could have corrupted Tom over the
decades and this has lead to him abusing Beverly

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.030
similar to how her father did.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:36.970
It could also be a reference to the source
material and 90s adaptation in which Pennywise

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:42.300
controls Tom and gets him to kidnap Bill's
wife and bring her to his lair as a hostage.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:46.090
Either way it's a really creepy image that
reminds us that you can't escape Derry no

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.150
matter how much you try got get away or forget.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.150
Henry Bowers
________________

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:53.040
When we are introduced to Henry Bowers we
can see in his room images of Pennywise on

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:57.300
the wall, most notably a red balloon which
shows that he never really got it out of his

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.300
head.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.300
The Restaurant
________________

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.380
I have seen a lot of comments on the last
video of people saying that Pennywise walks

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:06.390
behind the fish tank during the restaurant
scene but sorry everyone, I've watched it

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:09.700
about 5 times and still couldn't see it, honestly
you don't understand how many times I've seen

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.700
this film.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.700
The Bleachers
________________

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.310
Pennywise next pops up just before he makes
his attack on the young girl.

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:19.640
Similar to his attack on Georgie in the first
film, we can see It just before It makes it's

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:23.260
attack, sitting hiding in the background as
the girl chases the firefly.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.260
Mike's Vision
________________

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:28.700
The next major one we see appears during Mike's
vision of how to carry out the ritual of Chud.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:33.520
When viewing how IT came to Derry we can see
a form of Pennywise standing behind Mike mimicking

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:38.140
his movements and also in the scene we see
the original form that it used to attack the

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:42.300
Native Americans in the area which was a giant
bird and a huge beast.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:46.410
One of the forms for a split second looks
like the original Spider-form that is seen

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:51.501
at the end of the 1990 miniseries and in Mike's
room there's actually a poster with Pennywise

00:10:51.501 --> 00:10:54.320
on which is promoting the Derry Canal Days.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.360
There's no reason Mike would wanna have up
an image of the thing that scared him the

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.920
most throughout his entire life so I have
a sneaking suspicion that Pennywise put it

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.010
there himself.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:25.980
It Chapter 2 Everytime Pennywise Was In The
Background Of A Scene

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:26.980
Beverly's Token
________________

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:31.040
The next one is pretty obvious and was shown
in the teaser trailer for the film.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.380
This is Bob Gray who in the scene we discover
was a victim and alter ego that Pennywise

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.330
adopted at the start of the prior century
in Derry.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:42.080
This call back to the bottle from the previous
film is pretty nice and there's also some

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:46.320
hints that Pennywise is in the room just before
Beverly enters it including the door which

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:51.730
says Marsh before it changes to Kersh before
Beverly knocks and Bill Skarsgard's voice

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.675
which can be heard answering the door and
asking who's there.

00:11:53.675 --> 00:11:57.970
This shows that Pennywise probably made it's
play at the last second and jumped there,

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:00.260
creating the illusion just before Beverly
knocked.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:04.070
The old woman also pops her head round the
corner several times and does a walk like

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.020
when you get out of the shower without a towel.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.450
Richie At The Arcade
When Richie Revisits the arcade we can see

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:12.791
a torn poster behind him that has the words
'It' ripped into it and when the character

00:12:12.791 --> 00:12:18.160
goes outside he gets passed a Funeral Program
that not only has his face on it but also

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.920
Pennywise's on the back.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.839
It's a blink and you'll miss it moment that
lasts about a frame but it's another amazing

00:12:23.839 --> 00:12:24.839
little easter egg.

00:12:24.839 --> 00:12:25.839
Ben's Vision
________________

00:12:25.839 --> 00:12:30.100
When Ben revists the school we also get a
hint that Pennywise is infact using Beverly's

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:34.640
form as it's shadow appears infront of the
projector before there is seemingly a fake

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.610
out and we see that it's just Bev.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:40.760
In hindsight we know that this was indeed
the character, popping up to unnerve him before

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:44.970
quickly changing its form to try and get Ben
to let his guard down and even when we go

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:49.720
back to the shadow after he sees its Bev it
still looks exactly like Pennywise does.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:55.510
I guess you should never go to Summer School
or whenever this was that Ben attended whilst

00:12:55.510 --> 00:13:00.610
also fighting the creature, making friends
and building an underground bunker...yeah

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.060
some of these retcons don't work.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.060
pennywise in the background of scenes

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.060
The Fun Fair
________________

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.370
Anyway, when Bill chases the boy that now
lives in his old house at the funfair in order

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:10.330
to save him from the snatch of The Killer
Clown, we can see several elements of the

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:14.640
funhouse that feature the 1990s miniseries
Pennywise played by Tim Curry.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:19.360
They're not your typical punching bag as they
almost knock Bill off his feet when banging

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:23.010
into him showing that Pennywise always packs
a punch.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:27.530
Also before Bill finally catches up to the
kid Pennywise walks behind him at several

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:32.380
moments and even appears right over his shoulder
at one point.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:37.110
It's pretty scary and this scene definitely
holds a lot more weight knowing that Pennywise

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:40.220
was stalking him the entire time throughout
the house of mirrors.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.950
Yeah I'm never going in one again.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.110
Beverly In The Bathroom
________________

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:47.610
And finally at the end of The Movie when Beverly
is in the Bathroom, against the wall we can

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:52.560
see a graffiti version of Pennywise pressed
on the wall of the stall.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.960
This isn't in the stall in the first film
when Beverly sits in there and is tormented

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:58.990
by Greta the Bully so it looks like this was
later added by the creature in order to leave

00:13:58.990 --> 00:13:59.990
an impression.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:04.000
This crudely drawn kids version of the character
lets you know that Pennywise will always be

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:09.790
a part of Derry one way or another and is
a nice little squiggle that holds a lot more

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:11.450
weight to it than a simple drawing.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:17.960
We can also see the words 'Big is what It
Seems' which yeah, re-read it, 'Big is what

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:23.920
IT seems' which of course plays into the ending
of the movie in which they overcome the character

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.450
by showing that they are mentally stronger
than it.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:31.220
This final easter egg is a nod to Maturin,
the giant space turtle that is basically the

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:36.640
opposite of Pennywise that in the book helps
The Loser's Club defeat Pennywise by guiding

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:37.830
the characters psychically.

